f32 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2 and log2 of +-0, +-inf and NaN: NaN where f64 gives NaN, otherwise the signed zero or infinity f64 gives, or within the stated ulps of it (every backend): true
f32 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2 and log2 of finite nonzero inputs: within the stated ulps of f64 with subnormals kept (skipped on Metal and on CUDA's f32 intrinsics, accepted vendor behaviour claimed by their own contracts): true
Metal f32 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2 and log2: NaN where f64 gives NaN, the signed zero or infinity where f64 rounds to one, otherwise within the stated ulps of f64 -- for exp, log, exp2 and log2, of f64 at the input or the f32 result flushed from subnormal to zero: true
CUDA f32 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2 and log2 under --use_fast_math: within the fast intrinsics' contracts -- sin and cos absolute 2^-21.41 (plus 2^-23 |x| past pi) below 2^22 and any value in [-1, 1] from there, tanh relative 2^-10.987, exp 2 + 1.173 |x| ulps, log and log2 absolute 2^-21.41 and 2^-22 on [0.5, 2] and the stated ulps elsewhere, f32 subnormals flushed: true
half sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2 and log2 of +-0, +-inf and NaN: NaN where f64 gives NaN, otherwise the signed zero or infinity f64 gives, or within the stated ulps of it (every backend): true
half sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2 and log2 of finite nonzero inputs: within the stated ulps of f64 with subnormals kept (skipped on Metal and on CUDA's f32 intrinsics, accepted vendor behaviour claimed by their own contracts): true
Metal half sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2 and log2: NaN where f64 gives NaN, the signed zero or infinity where f64 rounds to one, otherwise within the stated ulps of f64 -- for exp, log, exp2 and log2, of f64 at the input or the f32 result flushed from subnormal to zero: true
bfloat16 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2 and log2 of +-0, +-inf and NaN: NaN where f64 gives NaN, otherwise the signed zero or infinity f64 gives, or within the stated ulps of it (every backend): true
bfloat16 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2 and log2 of finite nonzero inputs: within the stated ulps of f64 with subnormals kept (skipped on Metal and on CUDA's f32 intrinsics, accepted vendor behaviour claimed by their own contracts): true
Metal bfloat16 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2 and log2: NaN where f64 gives NaN, the signed zero or infinity where f64 rounds to one, otherwise within the stated ulps of f64 -- for exp, log, exp2 and log2, of f64 at the input or the f32 result flushed from subnormal to zero: true
CUDA bfloat16 sin, cos, tanh, exp, log, exp2 and log2 under --use_fast_math: within the fast intrinsics' contracts -- sin and cos absolute 2^-21.41 (plus 2^-23 |x| past pi) below 2^22 and any value in [-1, 1] from there, tanh relative 2^-10.987, exp 2 + 1.173 |x| ulps, log and log2 absolute 2^-21.41 and 2^-22 on [0.5, 2] and the stated ulps elsewhere, f32 subnormals flushed: true
f32 log and log2 have the sign of x - 1 on every f32 within 2^-13 of 1, and are +0 at 1 -- Box-Muller's sqrt (-2 log u) needs log u <= 0 (every backend): true
f32 log and log2 on every f32 within 2^-13 of 1: within the backend's contract -- the stated ulps of f64, CUDA's absolute 2^-21.41 and 2^-22 (every backend): true
